{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PrjtKmeXiy7vEZm24ZEzkm","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found information about Kafka Streams state stores preserving record headers configuration:\\\\n\\\\n## Answer\\\\n\\\\nAccording to **`/store/kips/KIP-1271.md`**, the Kafka Streams state stores **do preserve record headers configuration to cap maximum size of headers** in the final design. Specifically, the KIP mentions:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"The KIP introduces:\\\\n> - Header-aware store types\\\\n> - **A configuration to cap the size of headers written into state stores**\\\\n> - Ability to store and restore header-based metadata alongside values\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe KIP-1271 document states under \\\\\\\"Key Points\\\\\\\":\\\\n> \\\\\\\"- Introduces header-aware store types\\\\n> - **Small config to cap the size of headers written into state**\\\\n> - Preserves metadata with values in state stores\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis is also referenced in **`/store/pull-requests/21297.md`**, which is a proof-of-concept implementation, noting that KIP-1271 proposes:\\\\n> \\\\\\\"- Header-preserving state store types\\\\n> - **Configuration options for header size limits**\\\\n> - Separate store implementations (new vs legacy compatibility)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe feature allows storing header-based metadata (such as schema IDs, tracing information, and feature flags) in state stores, with a configuration parameter to limit the maximum size of headers to be stored.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"INDEX-WINDOW-15.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1271.md\\\",\\\"issues/KAFKA-20056.md\\\",\\\"pull-requests/21345.md\\\",\\\"pull-requests/21370.md\\\",\\\"pull-requests/21378.md\\\",\\\"WINDOW-17-2026-01-28-to-2026-01-29-summary.md\\\",\\\"WINDOW-18-2026-01-29-to-2026-01-31.md\\\",\\\"pull-requests/21297.md\\\",\\\"WINDOW-19-2026-01-31-summary.md\\\",\\\"INDEX-WINDOW-16.md\\\",\\\"I